# DevMemory credentials — copy to `.env` and fill in what you need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. The `devmemory` CLI loads it automatically (searched
# from the current directory upward). Real environment variables always win.
# Everything here is OPTIONAL — with nothing set, analysis uses the offline
# `rules` provider and analytics run against local SQLite.
#
# Non-secret settings (test command, metrics file, thresholds, catalog names)
# go in `.devmemory/config.json`, not here. See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.

# --- LLM analysis providers ---------------------------------------------------
# Add the matching provider name to `analysis.providers` in .devmemory/config.json
# (e.g. ["anthropic", "rules"]). Only the key for a configured provider is read.
#
# The "Ask" chat and `devmemory analyze` work with NO key:
#   - a built-in engine answers common questions from local data, always
#   - `pip install "devmemory-cli[local-llm]"` + `devmemory model pull` adds a
#     ~1 GB on-device LLM (Qwen2.5-Coder-1.5B) for open-ended questions, offline
# Set one of the keys below only to use a cloud model instead (it takes
# precedence over the on-device one; a Genie space below takes precedence over
# both). The cloud LLM writes a read-only SQL query against your local database.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter: one key, many models. Set analysis.providers = ["openrouter", "rules"]
# in config.json; for no-cost use set analysis.model to a "…:free" id
# (e.g. "minimax/minimax-m3:free"). A free Gemini key from Google AI Studio
# (GEMINI_API_KEY above) also works with providers = ["gemini", "rules"].
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY is accepted as a fallback for GEMINI_API_KEY
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- Databricks analytics sync ----------------------------------------------
# All three required. Also set `databricks.enabled = true` in config.json.
# `devmemory databricks push` publishes normalized telemetry (a 24-field
# allowlist) — never source, diffs, transcripts, or secrets.

DATABRICKS_HOST=
DATABRICKS_TOKEN=
DATABRICKS_WAREHOUSE_ID=

# Optional: a Genie space (reading the devmemory.analytics schema) that backs
# the dashboard's "Ask" chat at warehouse scale. Or set databricks.genie_space_id
# in config.json. Without this, Ask falls back to a local LLM (see above).
DATABRICKS_GENIE_SPACE_ID=

# --- misc ------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEBUG | INFO | WARNING (default: WARNING, or INFO with `devmemory -v`)
# DEVMEMORY_LOG_LEVEL=
